# 2. PROBLEM ONE — COMPLETE DUPLICATE NEWS ELIMINATION SYSTEM

This is one of the highest-priority problems.

Currently, the same news article sometimes appears four, five, or even ten times on the website.

This must be permanently fixed at the database and application levels.

## Requirements

Create an advanced News Deduplication Engine.

Every incoming article must be checked before it is stored or published.

Use multiple comparison methods:

- Normalized headline comparison.
- Hindi and English headline normalization.
- Unicode normalization.
- Whitespace and punctuation normalization.
- Removal of unnecessary special characters.
- Source URL comparison.
- Canonical URL comparison.
- News source and publication-time comparison.
- Semantic similarity comparison.
- Similarity checking between translated headlines.
- AI-assisted duplicate detection when appropriate.

For example:

"राजस्थान में किसानों के लिए बड़ी घोषणा"

"किसानों के लिए राजस्थान सरकार की बड़ी घोषणा"

These headlines may refer to the same story. The system should evaluate whether they are actually duplicates rather than treating every differently worded headline as a new story.

## Database-Level Protection

Create appropriate unique identifiers and duplicate-checking logic.

Requirements:

- One original news story should have one canonical record.
- Multiple sources reporting the same story should be associated with the canonical story instead of generating duplicate articles.
- Duplicate articles must not be published independently.
- Concurrent news-fetching jobs must not create duplicates.
- Database transactions and unique constraints must prevent race conditions.
- Repeated API calls must be idempotent.
- Rejected duplicate records should be logged for administration.

If two articles are genuinely different updates to the same developing event, allow them as separate updates only when they contain meaningful new information.

## Existing Duplicate Cleanup

Inspect existing articles and identify duplicates.

Create a safe cleanup migration:

1. Back up the existing article records.
2. Identify duplicate groups.
3. Preserve the most complete and reliable article.
4. Preserve useful images, sources, timestamps, and article details.
5. Merge useful information where appropriate.
6. Remove duplicate display records safely.
7. Recalculate article relationships and category references.
8. Verify that no valid independent news story was deleted.

Never automatically delete articles merely because their headlines contain similar words.

## Final Result

One news story = One canonical published article.

The same article must not appear repeatedly across the same listing or multiple automatically generated records.

